{title: Jeg løfter mine øyne mot fjellene}
{subtitle: Psalm 121}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I lift my eyes to the mountains
Where will my help come from
[Bb]My help comes from the [C]LORD
Who made [Gm]heaven and earth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He [Dm]will not let your [C]foot [Dm]slip
He who watches over [C]you will [Dm]not slum[Bb]ber
See, he who watches [C]over Israel
Will [Gm]neither slumber nor [Dm]sleep
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The [Bb]LORD watches [C]over you
[Dm]The LORD is your shade at your right side
[Bb]The sun will not strike you by [C]day
Nor the [Gm]moon by night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
The [Dm]LORD will keep you from [C]all [Dm]harm
He will watch over your [C][Dm]life
The [Bb]LORD will watch over [C]your going out and [Gm]your coming in
Now and forever[Dm]more
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] |
| [C] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
